        "summary": "Founded in 1987 by American businessman Richard Hartley, the Global Apex Wrestling emerged as the world's premier sports entertainment company during the cable television boom. Starting as a regional promotion in the Midwest, GAW rapidly expanded by acquiring smaller promotions and signing top talent globally. By the mid-1990s, it had established itself as the industry leader through innovative television programming, celebrity crossovers, and international expansion. Today, GAW operates two major brands (Thunder and Impact), hosts monthly premium events, and generates over $1 billion annually. Known for balancing athleticism with entertainment, GAW is the gold standard of mainstream professional wrestling.",
