        "summary": "Established in 1981 in Tokyo, Japan, King's Road Puroresu represents the pinnacle of traditional Japanese strong-style wrestling. Named after a famous wrestling territory in Kyoto, KRP was founded by wrestling legend Takeshi Yamamoto to preserve and elevate the puroresu tradition during Japan's wrestling boom. KRP is renowned for its hard-hitting style, stiff strikes, and storytelling through legitimate-looking athleticism. The promotion has produced numerous legendary wrestlers and maintains a devoted following across Asia and among puroresu enthusiasts worldwide. Despite smaller crowds than GAW, KRP commands fierce loyalty through its commitment to wrestling excellence and refusal to compromise artistic integrity for entertainment spectacle.",
