        "summary": "Established in 1992 as a successor to older Mexican wrestling traditions, Lucha Libre Internacional is Mexico's flagship promotion, based in Mexico City. LLI was founded by a consortium of lucha libre veterans who sought to modernize the mask wrestling tradition while preserving its cultural significance. Known for high-flying offense, masked warriors, and family dynasties, LLI hosts major events in historic arenas and maintains lucha libre's prominence in Mexican popular culture. While smaller than GAW, LLI is culturally significant throughout Latin America and has become a training ground for international wrestlers seeking to master the unique lucha libre style. The promotion emphasizes honor, legacy, and the sacred nature of the wrestler's mask.",
