        "summary": "Founded in 1975 in Manchester, England, British Stronghold Wrestling is Europe's oldest continuously operating wrestling promotion. BSW emerged from the UK's traditional catch wrestling lineage and built its reputation on technical grappling, mat wrestling, and strong style offense. Throughout the 1980s and 90s, BSW was a major regional power, but faced decline during the rise of American entertainment-focused wrestling. However, BSW experienced a revival in the 2010s through heritage marketing and a return to technical wrestling fundamentals. Today, BSW operates primarily in the UK and Europe, hosting weekly televised matches and quarterly premium events, attracting both nostalgia-driven older fans and a new generation of technical wrestling enthusiasts.",
